#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120672} :activity/id #uuid "6ede3e68-1ff6-5e3c-afed-499bb387f9a1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048499 :topic/id #uuid "a4bbeec2-7e3f-58f1-87d1-563d58d73752" :topic/math-academy-id 1851} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121034 :tutorial/content "Consider a vector $\\mathbf{u}$ which is given in terms of the vectors $\\mathbf{v_1}$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}+({\\color{red}-2}){\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}} = \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nHere, we say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a **linear combination** of the vectors ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}3}$ and ${\\color{red}-2}$ respectively. \n\nIn general, a linear combination of $n$ vectors $\\mathbf{v_1},\\mathbf{v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{v_n}$ is the *weighted sum*\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}x_1}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1}+{\\color{red}x_2}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2}+\\cdots + {\\color{red}x_n}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n} = \\mathbf{u},\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n}\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n}$ with coefficients (or *weights*) ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n},$ respectively.\n\nFor instance, \n![](images/ff/ff71636b9b5a34fec4de37b5e924c1c6bc3765c1ee823b325f5b0e01c0dc472a.svg)\nis the linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_3}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}2}, {\\color{red}0}, {\\color{red}\\dfrac{1}{2}},$ respectively." :tutorial/id #uuid "229ae855-226b-5f95-b050-b98257747800" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3186 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b14c637b-1418-59f5-9ac3-37a07d6ad580" :step/mat